          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.085,
            0.523,
            0.11
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "How many m is (a) 10 cm? (b) 15 cm?"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.119,
            0.389,
            0.154
          ],
          "content": "10   cm  = \\frac{1}{10}   m  = 0.1   m",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.157,
            0.845,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "Since each cm is one-hundredth of a meter, 15 cm can be written as"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.177,
            0.325,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "15   cm  = \\frac{15}{100}   m",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.216,
            0.344,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{10}{100}    m  + \\frac{5}{100}    m",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.255,
            0.332,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{10}    m  + \\frac{5}{100}    m",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.303,
            0.27,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "= 0 . 1 5 \\; \\mathrm { m } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.343,
            0.508,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "Fill in the blanks below (cm <–> m):"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.375,
            0.843,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "| 36 cm = _______ | 50 cm = _______ | _______ = 0.89 m |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 cm = _______ | 325 cm = _______ | ________ = 2.07 m |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_table_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.487,
            0.506,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "How many mm does 1 meter have?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.532,
            0.455,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": "Can we write 1 $\\mathrm{mm} = \\frac{1}{1000} \\mathrm{m}?$"
        },
        {
